 ## Key Design Decisions
 
 - **Commands over HTTPS, one authoritative board per event.** Editors submit commands to the server, which assigns each committed edit one event revision. Peer-to-peer or browser-side merging was rejected: the tenets require one authoritative revision regardless of delivery route, and offline editing is a non-goal.
+- **Self-hosted WebSockets for committed-change delivery.** Delivery pushes committed revisions to connected browsers over sockets the project operates itself, rather than five-second HTTPS polling or a hosted realtime service. Chosen for low-latency updates without recurring vendor fees or provider coupling, accepting the added cost of owning connection capacity and reconnect/catch-up logic. Polling was rejected for its repeated reads and seconds of lag; the hosted service was rejected for recurring fees and provider coupling.
